      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's natural to feel like you're burdening your children with your needs, and it's tempting to wonder if letting them break free would be more selfless. However, your children likely love and want to take care of you because it shows them that their family is a priority, and they're willing to make sacrifices to maintain that love and support. By letting them go, you'd be sacrificing the very thing that brings them comfort and reassurance - knowing they can take care of someone they love.",
